# Luxury · rich · compact

Every UI component must stay visually consistent: dense, refined, token-driven. Prefer existing project design tokens/CSS; if none, use a luxury-rich-compact language (tight spacing, soft surfaces, restrained accent, shared type scale).

## Rules
- Reuse existing layout shells, headers, tables, drawers, and controls — do not invent parallel design systems.
- No one-off hex palettes when theme tokens/variables exist.
- Compact density: short headers, tight padding, no sparse empty card chrome.
- Match nearest existing screen pattern for new components.
- Avoid generic AI defaults (purple gradients, oversized hero cards, pill/stat clutter) unless already brand-standard here.

